WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:10.404
Lander sends the fork's features on from obeya to obeya-outgoing, as clean branches for upstream. Some never go: the extension seam, and the extensions it carries, like Always allow.

00:00:11.358 --> 00:00:20.391
A quarantined feature has no Prepare for outgoing button at all, only Release from quarantine. The server refuses it as well, should a request come anyway.

00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:33.094
This feature passes the card count into the top bar's extension slot. That line calls the extensions, so preparing it for outgoing is refused, naming the file and the line: App dot T S X, line seven.

00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:44.544
This feature also edits a file on the seam list, the strings, but none of the lines that call the extensions. So it goes through: the agent ports it onto upstream's main as one clean commit.

00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:47.832
The branch is ready to push, without the seam.

00:00:48.785 --> 00:01:02.682
Upstream has meanwhile put a search into the top bar, right where the fork's extension slot sits. Syncing merges it into obeya and obeya-dev. The agent keeps the call into the extensions, and the outcome names each conflict at a seam call site.

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:09.404
So nothing of the seam leaves the fork, everyday features still do, and every sync keeps the seam intact.
